name: sim.writeTexture
description: Overwrites a specific texture (or a portion of it) with RGB data
luaSynopsis: sim.writeTexture(int textureId, int options, bytes textureData, int posX = 0, int posY = 0, int sizeX = 0, int sizeY = 0, float interpolation = 0)
pythonSynopsis: sim.writeTexture(int textureId, int options, buffer textureData, int posX = 0, int posY = 0, int sizeX = 0, int sizeY = 0, float interpolation = 0)
inputs:
1. textureId: ID of the texture. See also sim.getTextureId
2. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 reserved. Do not set
    - bit1 reserved. Do not set
    - bit2 set (4)=only an elliptical/circular portion of the texture data will be written
3. textureData: RGB data to write onto the texture. Each pixel is represented with 3 bytes (0-255)
4. posX / posY: x/y position where to copy the RGB data. Set to 0/0 to overwrite the full texture
5. sizeX / sizeY: x/y size of the RGB data. Set to 0/0 to overwrite the full texture
6. interpolation: fade or interpolation factor. 0 for no fade
outputs:
replacedBy:
- name: texture:set, class: mesh, file: mesh_texture_set.method
- name: texture:setData, class: mesh, file: mesh_texture_setData.method
